Also found the real root cause of the wiki bridge zero-artifact
bug: the CLI plugin loader uses a registration mode that noops
the memory capability registration. Posted a detailed trace on
GitHub. The previous theory (JSON serialization of function refs)
was wrong - the cache is an in-memory Map, not serialized JSON.
Getting the diagnosis right matters more than getting it fast.

